        "original_id": "b7c41836-5c0e-5e0b-ac57-71e43a64ebb1",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Bands: Catfish and the Bottlemen; The Lumineers\n- Albums and Songs: The Balcony; Stubborn Love\n- Places: Llandudno, Wales; Denver, Colorado; Ramsey, New Jersey\n- Topics: Rock; Folk rock; Americana\n\nFacts:\n- The Lumineers' members Schultz and Fraites began writing and performing together in Ramsey, New Jersey in 2005.\n- Catfish and the Bottlemen are a British rock band formed in Llandudno, Wales in 2007.\n- The Lumineers are an American folk rock/Americana band based in Denver, Colorado.\n- The Lumineers became one of the most popular folk rock/Americana artists during the revival and growing popularity of those genres in the 2010s.\n- The Balcony is the debut studio album by Welsh rock band Catfish and the Bottlemen.\n- \"Stubborn Love\" is a song by American folk rock band The Lumineers.",
